{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1176","t":"Hey Mohsin,\n\nHere's what I see on the chart.\n\nI have noted a little RBD and DBR within the down trend. I would consider these of lesser importance but if you extend them to the right you can see price reacting off of them as well. I've included them to show you that sometimes we get a longer base in our DBR/RBD. The two of note currently are the top and bottom ones limiting the current flag. I would put the base as the bottom of the candle on this one (the giant pin bar) as the next bar breaks away from it. That pin candle indicates a movement up then down which can also conceal a flag in the LTFs. On this TF I would consider it the base for simplicity's sake.\n\nYou can get crazy with drawing every blip on the chart and end up with something that will confuse the hell out of you:). For now the important DBR and RBD are the two that are limiting the flag. I indicated where I would think the FTB would be for those RBD/DBR. I also drew a blue box in with a new DBR that is a reaction to the main one. You could do the same for where I indicated FTB for the top one as well. This doesn't really give you any new info in this case other than that these areas are not fresh and we're waiting for a new decision to break one of the limits.\n\nDoes this answer your question? If not I'll try again. Cheers.","a":"antraxia","d":"","n":"#1176","p":48,"im":["f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11","1372bcb56e446bdd23f121b40bc194a18539aaee"],"m":1176},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1177","t":"oh yes you and mine (which was the idea given by RTM Marketpedia section) both have FTBs and there is nothing new in this case just inner marking","a":"mohsin360","d":"","n":"#1177","p":48,"im":[],"m":1177},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1178","t":"","a":"mohsin360","d":"","n":"#1178","p":48,"im":["0773b7ef8af79398a7152ba3cf06ba2d550e3ab9"],"m":1178},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1179","t":"Hye... this is the very first chart i have post here...","a":"Pengait FX","d":"","n":"#1179","p":48,"im":["4da44af4332c3237cc180a07d462230bacba4f76","cf40752d95cca16cfa6e0a13dd6a0146a107cbfe","b44b0af0ad0aca6b477634045a8f02fc22b053d7"],"m":1179},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1180","t":"Nice work, Pengait. Get abit more accurate/consistent with your box highs and lows and more features will become apparent to you.","a":"rcmacf","d":"","n":"#1180","p":48,"im":[],"m":1180},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1181","t":"Hi, my first homework","a":"fibreangel","d":"","n":"#1181","p":48,"im":["5917d0b5d5a9625bb27d7c7c001d8e0b33628d70","c4441168b98c71e9b8bea2fb810045fb72674699"],"m":1181},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1182","t":"Hello everyone,\n\nPlease feel free to let me know if I'm seeing this correctly, this is my first post and I just wanted to see if I'm heading in the right direction. DBR and RBD 1 of 200:)\n\nThanks, db","a":"db","d":"","n":"#1182","p":48,"im":["ff03ef6c2fdf946085a9f40948d1babd36b6d1ab"],"m":1182},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1183","t":"whiteout wrote: When looks messy, go on LTF Looks how different are the same messy on m30, and i have designed the zone approximately ecouse you have to do precisely:cheer: ]. Still a mess? Go on m15, then down.\n\nWhiteout, if it isn't too late to ask this question, when you mean do to LTF do you mean to draw the boxes more correctly or just to expand out the area?\n\nIncidentally, this is also my first post on RTM. I know I am at the right place. My gratitude knows no bounds.","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1183","p":48,"im":["ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a"],"m":1183},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1184","t":"My attempts at homework","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1184","p":48,"im":["98d574a7291deb1a31d7e904e8ac258bd639169c","dd6a8e04164f26fc55d0b412c2042882fd8116e7"],"m":1184},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1185","t":"My charts look quite hazy. Dont know why. I took the screenshot through Shotty, edited through Snaggit, converted from png to jpeg using Paint. Somewhere down the line the quality got zapped.:(","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1185","p":48,"im":[],"m":1185},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1186","t":"My attempt at Cap/DBR + RBD homework.","a":"DrummerBoy","d":"","n":"#1186","p":48,"im":["54600faf61e18a44e0c46ff6441ce9a2a3d8f6e2"],"m":1186},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1187","t":"I think Whiteout means that if the area looks \"messy\", it would look more clear at a lower time frame. For example, for the chart above, you'd go down to M15 or M5 timeframe. No worries about being your first post. We all have to start somewhere, and we are all here to learn.","a":"DrummerBoy","d":"","n":"#1187","p":48,"im":[],"m":1187},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1188","t":"Thanks Drummer Boy.\n\nHere is another chart from me.","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1188","p":48,"im":["0d7500ae4cebb32895fcfba746609352f7d95442"],"m":1188},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1189","t":"","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1189","p":48,"im":["64e299e3ae237d41c8a76ef1e776dc3407206899","6cf269a466063a88f57fad5f2213412f8a2db878"],"m":1189},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1190","t":"4H perspective of the above chart, seems to be an ABC correction after the downmove thats been on for so long","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1190","p":48,"im":["0041cd8ad58fa19bb900e0091f4e4218e7e628cd"],"m":1190},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1191","t":"The same chart as above highlighting the decision made to break out of the trading range area (Flag Limit)","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1191","p":48,"im":["dd510034707c239c48b7493ad71eeca0a9157684"],"m":1191},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1192","t":"another one. this time sticking to the topic and not getting carried away:)","a":"winnertrader","d":"","n":"#1192","p":48,"im":["d77d709d4984a81ffb24d8736510696f7a76b83b"],"m":1192},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1193","t":"Hi everyone, here is my first chart i hope that i didn`t misunderstand this asignment","a":"arnoud","d":"","n":"#1193","p":48,"im":["25f7a3da38501f866fa21e976c900ce657f4408f"],"m":1193},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1194","t":"arnoud wrote: Hi everyone, here is my first chart i hope that i didn`t misunderstand this asignment\n\nHi Arnoud, Since this is a forum for DBR and RBD, I believe the purpose of the homework is to validate the reaction of price when it returns to the base. I added my two cents on your chart. Good luck. I am learning as well, so if I am off, feel free to correct.:)","a":"DrummerBoy","d":"","n":"#1194","p":48,"im":["534cc4d6ffb9182e26d49c6f53d08122ec696591"],"m":1194},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1195","t":"First go, Hopefully not too bad. Any comments welcome\n\nregards Sm0uvy","a":"sm0uvy","d":"","n":"#1195","p":48,"im":["e7a60bb16870dece33738693f028f9b65e034cd7"],"m":1195},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1196","t":"Okay, let's put the pieces together. First homework, here it comes: GBPUSD Daily\n\nEURJPY H4\n\nCrude Oil H1\n\nI hope this looks okay, comments are always appreciated\n\nThanks in advance!","a":"thetrendsfriend","d":"","n":"#1196","p":48,"im":["478122dae49d1ecebab38783de1b4429dde8a01c","350d46064e254735e87003d715ac8142f2f0fb3b","1d65a5692cd3c049f1712f30bde15520da2da4f5"],"m":1196},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1197","t":"Hey there, Friend. Just some guidance as you start out. Good effort thus far","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#1197","p":48,"im":["fe9ca357ed0ed1c6184e68edd6ae5edbc2449015","abe91fde41c3c51fa1f844f575affd0d8e557126"],"m":1197},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1198","t":"naascott wrote: Hey there, Friend. Just some guidance as you start out. Good effort thus far\n\nThanks for the feedback! So do you think it would be better to change to weekly charts to see the larger movements? The problem I already thought of is, that there's always something left, until 19xx:) My primary aim was just to look at different timeframes while doing the homework.","a":"thetrendsfriend","d":"","n":"#1198","p":48,"im":["fe9ca357ed0ed1c6184e68edd6ae5edbc2449015"],"m":1198},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1199","t":"Hi\n\nLooking at GBPUSD and trying to workout where it is going next. Looked at H1, m15 and m1. Put in the DBR's and the RBD's, but can't see where it is going to go next. I can't see any signals giving me a clue. Thanks for any help.\n\nregards sm0uvy","a":"sm0uvy","d":"","n":"#1199","p":48,"im":["fe58479607b4080e9d0f55856cb08f2cf34f4844","ce4548a3be2367507d6be67a25716042621cac39","1e489e4fe443d1083583c56d7995819a2175e5d5"],"m":1199},{"id":"dbrrbd_p48_1200","t":"Hi,\n\nI think i might have answered my own question.\n\nI should have waited for a clear signal.\n\nIs this correct?\n\nregards sm0uvy\n\n434445464748495051","a":"sm0uvy","d":"","n":"#1200","p":48,"im":["f3ef0927e095370d37e0d18b6ac6c7c7c45a4e71"],"m":1200}],"images":[{"k":"ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a","t":"assets/thumbs/ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a.webp","f":"assets/images/ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a.jpeg","w":1276,"h":631,"b":88772,"o":"ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a.jpeg","p":48,"pid":"dbrrbd_p48_1183"},{"k":"f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11","t":"assets/thumbs/f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11.webp","f":"assets/images/f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11.jpeg","w":96,"h":144,"b":3559,"o":"f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11.jpeg","p":48,"pid":"dbrrbd_p48_1176"},{"k":"1372bcb56e446bdd23f121b40bc194a18539aaee","t":"assets/thumbs/1372bcb56e446bdd23f121b40bc194a18539aaee.webp","f":"assets/images/1372bcb56e446bdd23f121b40bc194a18539aaee.jpeg","w":1422,"h":528,"b":97958,"o":"1372bcb56e446bdd23f121b40bc194a18539aaee.jpeg","p":48,"pid":"dbrrbd_p48_1176"},{"k":"0773b7ef8af79398a7152ba3cf06ba2d550e3ab9","t":"assets/thumbs/0773b7ef8af79398a7152ba3cf06ba2d550e3ab9.webp","f":"assets/images/0773b7ef8af79398a7152ba3cf06ba2d550e3ab9.jpeg","w":568,"h":338,"b":25782,"o":"0773b7ef8af79398a7152ba3cf06ba2d550e3ab9.jpeg","p":48,"pid":"dbrrbd_p48_1178"},{"k":"4da44af4332c3237cc180a07d462230bacba4f76","t":"assets/thumbs/4da44af4332c3237cc180a07d462230bacba4f76.webp","f":"assets/images/4da44af4332c3237cc180a07d462230bacba4f76.png","w":1200,"h":800,"b":18460,"o":"4da44af4332c3237cc180a07d462230bacba4f76.png","p":48,"pid":"dbrrbd_p48_1179"},{"k":"cf40752d95cca16cfa6e0a13dd6a0146a107cbfe","t":"assets/thumbs/cf40752d95cca1